Explanation of the change:

- We detect the two “end” coordinates in screen‐pixel space.
- We compute their pixel‐distance and multiply by the current view’s resolution (map units per pixel).
- We feed that “true” map‐unit radius back into `setCenterAndRadius`.
- The result: your drawn circle stays circular on screen in both EPSG:3857 and EPSG:4326/useGeographic modes.
